pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Companion to `add.pbp`, NOT run by the gate: the same checker and the same `add.opb`,
% with a logged model. It answers `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE`, exit 0, before and after the
% fix. One checker, one formula, both verdicts -- so `add.pbp`'s `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE`
% is visibly false without trusting any second tool.
%
% It is also the guard against a bogus fix: a "fix" that made the checker refuse rows with
% extreme degrees outright would pass the negative test and break this one.
f 1 ;
sol x1 ~x2 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
